# CP-0 — Integrity / verification tool

This is an integrity/verification tool. All logic in the trust path must be deterministic and unit-testable.

- Never add an LLM call, a heuristic score, a probabilistic classifier, or a network request the user did not explicitly request.
- Never implement an evaluation metric, scorer, or "assessment framework" — this project verifies evaluations, it never performs them.
- Never receive, store, or transmit a user's dataset, model, prompts, or outputs; digests and metadata only.
- Never add a flag, env var, or code path that permits overriding a sealed decision rule.
- Never make our log the only endpoint that can verify an attestation.
- Never use a dependency not already in go.mod without asking first. Prefer the standard library.
